        "original_id": "3bc42e68-871c-5183-af37-7427902ab464",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marc Rosset, Max Mirnyi, Jonathan Erlich, Andy Ram, Renzo Furlan, Feliciano López, Fernando Verdasco\n- Events: 1992 Olympic Games, 1994 Waldbaum's Hamlet Cup – Singles, 2009 Australian Open – Men's Doubles\n- Places: Switzerland, Minsk, Belarus\n- Topics: professional tennis, defending champions, injuries\n\nFacts:\n- Marc Rosset was born on 7 November 1970 and is a former professional tennis player from Switzerland.\n- Marc Rosset is best remembered for winning the men's singles gold medal at the 1992 Olympic Games.\n- At the 1994 Waldbaum's Hamlet Cup – Singles, defending champion Marc Rosset lost in the second round to Renzo Furlan.\n- Max Mirnyi was born on 6 July 1977 in Minsk and is a Belarusian professional tennis player.\n- At the 2009 Australian Open – Men's Doubles, Jonathan Erlich and Andy Ram were the defending champions.\n- At the 2009 Australian Open – Men's Doubles, Jonathan Erlich did not participate because of an elbow injury.\n- At the 2009 Australian Open – Men's Doubles, Andy Ram partnered with Max Mirnyi and lost in the second round to Feliciano López and Fernando Verdasco.",
